  "mapping": {
    "slotKey": "lowercase(nameId) minus a leading 'mod_' minus a trailing '_<digits>'; 'pistol*' collapses to 'pistol_grip'. Identical to PilotHubBuilder.slotKey so the two layers can never disagree.",
    "rules": [
      "1. Candidates = archetypes whose fitsSlots contains the slot's slotKey.",
      "2. +100 if the item's category name (or any ancestor category name) is in categoryMatch.",
      "3. +60 per keyword found in the item's lowercased name or short name - MORE than a category hit, because Tarkov files a 60-round drum under the same plain \"Magazine\" category as a STANAG box, so only the name can separate them.",
      "4. + priority, as the tiebreak when two archetypes score identically on category and keywords.",
      "4b. PLATFORM GATE: an archetype carrying a `platform` only matches a gun with the same `platform` (ar | ak), so an AR handguard can never land on an AK and an AK dust cover can never land on an M4. Archetypes with no `platform` (optics, foregrip, light) are shared on purpose.",
      "4c. CALIBER GATE: an archetype carrying `calibers` only matches a gun whose `caliber` is in that list. Magazines carry it; nothing else needs to.",
      "5. Best score wins; a score of 0 is NOT a match.",
      "6. No match, or no archetype for the slot at all => render the labelled ghost box at the socket. Nothing ever fails to render.",
      "7. An EMPTY slot uses guns[id].defaultParts[nameId] when present, so the gun always reads as a complete weapon.",
      "8. A gun id with no entry in `guns` has no 3D at all - the viewer reports supports(gunId)=false and the 3D toggle must be hidden for it."
    ],
    "fallback": "ghost"
  },
  "ghost": {
    "size": [
      0.075,
      0.055,
